# fortran-names.d/2026-11-05-step44b-tab-bar -- the names step 44b (tab-bar.el)
# gives Lisp-derived terms, by existing rules and precedents (decided and
# reported): the history commands verb first (R6-17, R6-40) after
# xref-go-back -> go_back_in_xref_history; the commands each a name of
# their own, the long name verb, package, rest (decision 48 Q1: tab-bar-close-tab ->
# close_tab_bar_tab) and each alias verb first from its own words
# (tab-close -> close_tab, tab-next -> next_tab after smerge-next), as
# every upstream alias is ported (vc_pull and vc_update).
# tab-bar-new-tab and tab-bar-new-tab-to (make_tab_bar_tab,
# make_tab_bar_tab_to) and tab-group (change_tab_group) have no entry: as
# runs of parts they are in the options tab_bar_new_tab_to (an option of
# the same name), tab_bar_new_tab_choice and tab_bar_new_tab_group, and
# in tab_bar_tab_group_current and the other group names.
#
